  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/johannes-schmieder/fevc/zipball/v0.5.2",
  "body": "fevc 0.5.2 enables automatic and explicit shared full-CMG estimation on Windows, including supported projection and component-inference routes. It also avoids redundant result exports and unnecessary serial scheduling overhead. Exact and explicit diagonal routing, scientific tolerances, cancellation and caller-state restoration retain their contracts.\n\nAll five plugins are built from `ec5e1e0ec4428d7a4410c7ce4d2709df006a8da4` with unmodified CMG `e5613e81fb3b03c78de98658b372646fa802aabb` and explicit 128 levels. Mac arm64/Rosetta, SCC Linux, hosted Windows/MSRV checks and all 18 private Windows qualification groups pass. All 12 registered scientific and complete-command performance cells pass; all 144 timings and earlier failed/development results are preserved.\n\nThe assets include the installation ZIP, exact corresponding source, binary/source inventory and SHA-256 checksums. Install the tagged package with:\n\n```stata\nnet install fevc, replace from(\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/johannes-schmieder/fevc/v0.5.2/\")\n```\n\nRestart Stata after replacement to load the new plugin. Windows runtime qualification covers one/two workers and the declared fixtures. Mac x86-64 runtime testing uses Rosetta; native Intel hardware, representative-scale performance and general statistical coverage are not claimed.\n"
